sequenceDiagram
  participant G as Grove
  participant N as Runner (job, terminal, launch events)
  participant X as harness-dispatch beside Grove
  participant P as Owner policy
  participant H as Harness
  Note over G,H: Lifecycle session: bare grove
  G->>G: Create a fresh launch directory, activate the epoch with its path
  G->>N: run --kind --task-file --task-id --prompt --exit-dir --ending-file, no parameter
  N->>X: Spawn in the working-tree root as a job, GROVE_LAUNCH_DIR set
  X->>P: select(request), cwd = working-tree root
  alt Policy refuses, or no policy
    X-->>N: Diagnostic + remedy + inspect line on the terminal, nonzero exit, no ending
    N-->>G: Reaped: the loop stops, the leaf stays live
  else Command selected
    X->>H: Record the run, spawn the harness as dispatch's own job
    opt Finish session that tore the grove down
      H->>G: grove-llm record-teardown writes the teardown record
    end
    H->>X: harness-dispatch exit, the exit signal
    X->>H: Escalate, end its group, reap, restore the terminal
    X-->>N: End observation recorded, ending file written, exit
    N-->>G: Reaped: read the teardown record and the ending
  end
  Note over G,H: Standalone invocation: grove run KIND
  G->>G: Stage the private working directory
  G->>N: run --confine --kind --prompt --runtime-read --ending-file, noninteractively
  N->>X: Spawn in the staged directory, own session, output to the transcript
  X->>P: select(request), outside the sandbox, with the owner's grants
  X->>H: Record the run, spawn confined: small environment, run ID, exit channel
  H->>X: Outputs written, then harness-dispatch exit by its canonical path
  X-->>N: exit_signal ending, exit 0
  N-->>G: Publish the declared outputs
